    "q-44742": {
      "dom_id": "step-q44742",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Represent the solution of the inequality $4x+2\\le 10$ on a number line.",
      "worked_solution": "First, we apply the addition principle, subtracting $2$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+2 & \\le 10 \\\\ 4x+2-2 & \\le 10-2 \\\\ 4x+0 & \\le 8 \\\\ 4x & \\le 8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSecond, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by $4:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x & \\le 8 \\\\ \\frac{4x}{4} & \\le \\frac{8}{4} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{4}x}{\\cancel{4}} & \\le \\frac{8}{4} \\\\ x & \\le 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the solution is $x\\le 2.$ The solution can be expressed on a number line, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14192536/assets/b02bead6d12049fedcf78bea9558a7c95ee85d78f801e41c46ea653ba1712750.png)",
